 "notes": [
  "Monster levels, XP and stats (PLAN-LEVELING.md 2 and 6, PLAN-CREATURES.md; NOTES.md 'Stat effects and monster tuning'). Read by game/leveling.cpp and game/stat_effects.cpp; only used with Leveling on.",
  "One level per type (PLAN-CREATURES.md, 2026-11-07): 'level' is the type's level and its stats. Where the original places a type on a map whose story stage is below that level, 'maps' keeps the weaker variant that map had, shown with 'weak_prefix' ('young troll', 'lesser ghost'): the same sprite, other stats. Maps not listed get the type's level. A spawned monster keeps its level (saved with it).",
  "Stats: hp [lo, hi], dex [lo, hi], str (damage + STR/5, as the Avatar's weapon blows), int (spell damage x (1 + (INT-10)/20) for casters), damage [lo, hi]. Armour and damage / defence types stay the original table's. hp and damage were tuned with tests/test_balance.cpp (mode tune) to the plan's targets; DEX follows a level-N Avatar's DEX, shifted by the type's own, at most 24.",
  "xp by level 1..8: 1, 2, 3, 5, 22, 24, 152, 176 (fire skulls 30%), the same for every type of a level (the late levels raised once more for one level per type: the late maps now hold lower-level types; checked by test_leveling's budget and pacing, which also count data/creatures.json). Paid in full to the Avatar and every companion walking with him, once per body. Peasants, children and guards pay nothing. A shape not listed pays nothing and keeps its original stats.",
  "level_difference_percent: what a kill pays, by (earner's level - monster's level); the last value repeats for anything further below. Never less than 1 XP."
 ],
